{
	"id": "g4.maths.decimals",
	"lesson": [
		{
			"text": "Quick memory: last unit, fractions times whole numbers. What is 3 × 1/4? 3/4: 3 lots of one quarter."
		},
		{
			"text": "A tenth is 1 of 10 equal parts. 3/10 is written 0.3 as a decimal: the first place after the point is tenths.",
			"picture": {
				"kind": "bar",
				"den": 10,
				"num": 3
			}
		},
		{
			"text": "A hundredth is 1 of 100 equal parts. 45/100 is 0.45: 4 tenths and 5 hundredths.",
			"picture": {
				"kind": "bar",
				"den": 100,
				"num": 45
			}
		},
		{
			"text": "1 tenth is 10 hundredths, so 3/10 = 30/100. That lets us add them: 3/10 + 4/100 = 30/100 + 4/100 = 34/100."
		},
		{
			"text": "To compare decimals, compare the tenths first: 0.5 > 0.45 because 5 tenths are more than 4 tenths. 0.5 and 0.50 are equal.",
			"picture": {
				"kind": "number_line",
				"from": "0",
				"to": "1",
				"step": "0.1",
				"marks": [
					"0.45",
					"0.5"
				],
				"labels": "ends"
			}
		},
		{
			"text": "Try it in the world: build a wall of 10 blocks and colour 3 of them: 0.3 of the wall. Then a 10 by 10 floor with 45 coloured: 0.45. Next: measuring and converting."
		}
	],
